{"id":"bdb/Breakpoint","module":"bdb","qualname":"Breakpoint","name":"Breakpoint","kind":"class","parent":null,"signatures":["Breakpoint(self, file, line, temporary=False, cond=None, funcname=None)"],"doc":"Breakpoint class.\n\nImplements temporary breakpoints, ignore counts, disabling and\n(re)-enabling, and conditionals.\n\nBreakpoints are indexed by number through bpbynumber and by\nthe (file, line) tuple using bplist.  The former points to a\nsingle instance of class Breakpoint.  The latter points to a\nlist of such instances since there may be more than one\nbreakpoint per line.\n\nWhen creating a breakpoint, its associated filename should be\nin canonical form.  If funcname is defined, a breakpoint hit will be\ncounted when the first line of that function is executed.  A\nconditional breakpoint always counts a hit.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/bdb.html#bdb.Breakpoint","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":[],"source":{"path":"Lib/bdb.py","line":969},"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
